  "summary": "A flow nozzle is a differential-pressure flow element with a smooth, curved inlet leading to a cylindrical throat. It is more robust than an orifice plate and handles high-velocity, high-temperature and erosive flows such as boiler steam and feedwater, with a lower permanent loss than an orifice but higher than a venturi (ISO 5167-3).",
